estigates the prevalence of sarcopenia in community-dwelling older people in the UK.", "ELLI STUDY:The ELLI study investigates the prevalence of sarcopenia in patients attending outpatient geriatric clinics. It focuses on understanding how common this condition is among the elderly population receiving care in these settings.", "INTERNATIONAL SARCOPENIA INITIATIVE:The International Sarcopenia Initiative (EWGSOP and IWGS) conducts systematic reviews on sarcopenia in aging adults.", "ENGLISH LONGITUDINAL STUDY OF AGEING:The English Longitudinal Study of Ageing provides findings on the prevalence of frailty and disability among older adults.", "FRAILTY AND DEPENDENCE IN ALBACETE STUDY:The Frailty and Dependence in Albacete study assesses the prevalence of frailty in a Spanish elderly population.", "SURVEY OF HEALTH, AGEING AND RETIREMENT IN EUROPE:The SHARE study compares patterns of frailty in older adults across different income countries.", "STUDY ON GLOBAL AGEING AND ADULT HEALTH:The SAGE study focuses on global aging and health issues affecting older adults.", "AMERICAN JOURNAL OF EPIDEMIOLOGY:The American Journal of Epidemiology publishes studies on the epidemiology of sarcopenia among the elderly.", "JOURNAL OF NUTRITION HEALTH AND AGING:The Journal of Nutrition Health and Aging publishes research on the prevalence of sarcopenia in community-dwelling elderly.", "CLINICAL GERIATRIC MEDICINE:Clinical Geriatric Medicine discusses the pathogenesis and management of sarcopenia.", "ILSIRENTE STUDY:The ilSIRENTE study examines the relationship between sarcopenia and mortality risk in frail older persons aged 80 years and older."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}